To find the probability that exactly 4 out of 7 islands have treasure, we can use the binomial probability formula. The formula for the probability of getting exactly \( k \) successes in \( n \) trials, where each trial has a success probability \( p \), is given by: \[ P(X = k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k} \] In this case: - \( n = 7 \) (the number of islands), - \( k = 4 \) (the number of islands with treasure), - \( p = \frac{1}{5} \) (the probability of finding treasure on an island). First, calculate the binomial coefficient \(\binom{7}{4}\): \[ \binom{7}{4} = \frac{7!}{4!(7-4)!} = \frac{7!}{4!3!} = \frac{7 \times 6 \times 5 \times 4!}{4! \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = \frac{7 \times 6 \times 5}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 35 \] Next, calculate \( p^k \) and \( (1-p)^{n-k} \): \[ p^k = \left( \frac{1}{5} \right)^4 = \frac{1}{625} \] \[ (1-p)^{n-k} = \left( \frac{4}{5} \right)^3 = \frac{64}{125} \] Now, substitute these values into the binomial probability formula: \[ P(X = 4) = 35 \times \frac{1}{625} \times \frac{64}{125} \] Simplify the expression: \[ P(X = 4) = 35 \times \frac{64}{78125} = \frac{2240}{78125} \] Therefore, the probability that exactly 4 of the islands have treasure is \(\boxed{\frac{2240}{78125}}\).
[Final answer] \frac{2240}{78125}

